{#
label/_form.html.twig — create/edit a label inside the modal frame.

Delegates to _partials/_modal_form.html.twig, which supplies the
<turbo-frame id="modal"> wrapper Turbo needs to render the response. Without
that frame the fetch finds nothing to swap and the modal stays empty — the
account form (account/_form_modal.html.twig) does the same thing by hand.

Field styling comes from the global form theme
(_layout/form/modal_form_theme.html.twig), so the widgets render bare here.

Embedded rather than included, for the delete control below: it needs the
shell's `after_fields` slot, and an include cannot fill a block.
#}
{% extends '_layout/app.html.twig' %}

{% block body %}
    {% embed '_partials/_modal_form.html.twig' with {
        form: form,
        label: label,
        title: label.id is null ? 'sidebar.labels.add'|trans : 'label.form.edit_title'|trans,
    } only %}
        {#
        Deleting a label, from the dialog that edits it.

        The route has existed all along and settings has offered it all along —
        the gap was that the dialog the sidebar's pencil opens did not, and the
        sidebar is where a label is actually lived with. Someone editing a label
        they no longer want had to know to go and look in a settings panel.

        Below the fields and under a rule, not beside Save. The footer holds the
        two buttons that finish the dialog the way it was opened for; this is a
        different act with a different outcome, and putting a destructive verb
        next to the primary one is how it gets pressed by muscle memory. It says
        what it will do before it does it, and then asks.

        `formaction` rather than a <form> of its own, because this markup sits
        INSIDE the label form and nested forms are not a thing — the browser
        drops the inner one and the button silently posts the label edit
        instead. `formnovalidate` so a cleared Name field cannot block a delete;
        the fields are irrelevant to a row that is about to be removed.
        #}
        {% block after_fields %}
            {% if label.id is not null and not label.isSystem %}
                <div class="pt-5 border-t border-line space-y-2.5">
                    <p class="text-[13px] leading-snug text-ink-muted">
                        {{ 'label.form.delete_hint'|trans }}
                    </p>

                    <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token('label-delete' ~ label.id) }}">

                    <button
                        type="submit"
                        formmethod="post"
                        formnovalidate
                        formaction="{{ path('app_label_delete', { id: label.id }) }}"
                        data-turbo-confirm="{{ label.children|length > 0
                            ? 'label.delete_confirm_children'|trans({ '%name%': label|label_name, '%count%': label.children|length })
                            : 'label.delete_confirm'|trans({ '%name%': label|label_name }) }}"
                        class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 h-8 px-3.5 rounded-lg text-sm font-medium
                           text-danger
                           bg-transparent
                           border border-danger/40
                           hover:bg-danger-soft
                           focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-red-500 focus-visible:ring-offset-1
                           transition-colors duration-100"
                    >
                        <i class="fa-solid fa-trash text-xs" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                        {{ 'label.form.delete'|trans }}
                    </button>
                </div>
            {% endif %}
        {% endblock %}
    {% endembed %}
{% endblock %}
